@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Notice - Common Understanding";
}

<nav aria-label="breadcrumb" class="cu-breadcrumb">
    <ol class="breadcrumb">
        <li class="breadcrumb-item">
            <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Index"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Home</a>
        </li>
        <li class="breadcrumb-item active" aria-current="page">Privacy Notice</li>
    </ol>
</nav>

<h1 class="cu-page-heading"><i class="fas fa-shield-alt"></i> Privacy Notice</h1>

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
        <div class="cu-card mb-4">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> What This Notice Covers</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <p class="lead">Common Understanding helps people explore beliefs, compare arguments, and build a shared understanding graph.</p>
                <p>This notice describes the information processed by the web application, why it is processed, and the limits of the privacy protections currently implemented. It describes the current system, not a future architecture.</p>
                <div class="alert alert-warning">
                    <i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
                    <strong>AI-assisted features use service providers.</strong> Prompts, submitted arguments, and other text needed for an AI-assisted feature may be processed by an external provider acting on behalf of the service. Do not submit information that you are not comfortable having processed for that purpose.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cu-card mb-4">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-database"></i> Information the System Stores</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <p>Depending on how you use the service, records may include:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Account credentials, display name, account identifier, and authentication records.</li>
                    <li>Discovery responses, belief signals, worldview snapshots, forecasts, and related interaction history.</li>
                    <li>Arguments, replies, votes, debates, connections, badges, and feed preferences.</li>
                    <li>Evidence, source and provenance information, imported reference material, and relationships between contributions.</li>
                    <li>Security, request, error, performance, and feature-engagement telemetry used to operate and protect the service.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mb-0">Some contributions are published as public content and can appear in feeds, comparisons, embedded experiences, or the Understanding Graph. Account and profile data is used according to the access rules for the relevant feature.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cu-card mb-4">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-cogs"></i> How Information Is Used</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <ul>
                    <li>To provide discovery, analysis, graph exploration, social discussion, debate, recommendations, and related features.</li>
                    <li>To generate structured classifications, summaries, comparisons, and other analysis requested by the service.</li>
                    <li>To publish and connect public contributions when a feature is designed to be public.</li>
                    <li>To authenticate users, enforce authorization, prevent abuse, investigate suspicious activity, and maintain service integrity.</li>
                    <li>To diagnose failures, measure performance, and improve the reliability and quality of the application.</li>
                    <li>To meet legal obligations or respond to valid legal and safety requests.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mb-0">The service does not treat AI-generated classifications or summaries as facts. They are derived outputs that may be reviewed, disputed, corrected, or replaced as the system and its data change.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cu-card mb-4">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-share-alt"></i> Service Providers and Data Movement</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <p>We use service providers to host, store, secure, monitor, and deliver the application, and to provide some AI-assisted features. These providers may process submitted content and limited technical information only as needed to provide those services, protect the platform, or meet legal obligations.</p>
                <p>Information processed by a provider may be handled outside the application itself and may be subject to the provider's infrastructure locations and contractual safeguards. We do not sell personal information or provide submitted content to service providers for their own advertising.</p>
                <p class="mb-0">The application uses essential cookies to keep users signed in and protect account sessions. These cookies expire or are renewed according to the service's session settings.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cu-card mb-4">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-lock"></i> Security, Retention, and Deletion</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <ul>
                    <li>Access to account features is authenticated and authorization is checked for protected resources.</li>
                    <li>Administrative, organizational, and technical safeguards are used to protect information in transit and at rest. Safeguards may vary by operating environment and service provider.</li>
                    <li>Records are retained for as long as needed to provide the feature, preserve public contributions and graph relationships, maintain security and service history, meet legal obligations, or resolve disputes. This notice does not claim a universal 90-day deletion or anonymization schedule.</li>
                    <li>Deleting an account or contribution may affect public discussions, votes, graph relationships, derived analysis, backups, audit records, and other users. Deletion is therefore handled through the applicable account or administration workflow and may require removal or anonymization across related records.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mb-0">No security measure eliminates all risk. Please avoid submitting passwords, financial information, health information, or other sensitive personal information unless the feature and its purpose clearly require it.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cu-card mb-4">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-hand-paper"></i> Your Requests</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <p>Subject to applicable law and the system's public-content and security obligations, you may ask the administrator to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Explain what information associated with your account is held and how it is used.</li>
                    <li>Correct inaccurate account or contribution information where the relevant workflow permits correction.</li>
                    <li>Review a request to delete or anonymize personal information, including the effect on public or shared records.</li>
                    <li>Review an AI-generated classification or analysis that you believe is inaccurate or misleading.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="mb-0">The current application does not provide self-service export or account-deletion buttons from this page. Requests should be sent through the platform's identified administrator or support channel, with enough information to locate the relevant account or record. Do not send a password.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cu-card">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-envelope"></i> Questions and Requests</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <p>For privacy questions, correction requests, deletion requests, or concerns about a public contribution, contact the Common Understanding platform administrator through the support channel provided to you for this deployment.</p>
                <div class="alert alert-info mb-0">
                    <i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i>
                    <strong>Important:</strong> The address previously shown on this page was a placeholder, not a monitored privacy office. Do not rely on it for a privacy request.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-lg-4">
        <div class="cu-card">
            <div class="cu-card-header"><i class="fas fa-key"></i> Privacy Highlights</div>
            <div class="cu-card-body">
                <ul class="list-unstyled mb-0">
                    <li class="mb-3"><i class="fas fa-cloud text-primary"></i> <strong>Service providers</strong><br /><small class="text-muted">Selected providers support hosting, operations, security, and AI-assisted features.</small></li>
                    <li class="mb-3"><i class="fas fa-microchip text-warning"></i> <strong>AI-assisted processing</strong><br /><small class="text-muted">Text needed for an AI-assisted feature may be processed outside the application.</small></li>
                    <li class="mb-3"><i class="fas fa-globe text-info"></i> <strong>Public contributions</strong><br /><small class="text-muted">Content marked public may be visible to other users and connected features.</small></li>
                    <li class="mb-0"><i class="fas fa-user-lock text-success"></i> <strong>Protected account data</strong><br /><small class="text-muted">Authentication and feature authorization restrict protected records.</small></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-light mt-4">
            <small class="text-muted"><i class="fas fa-clock"></i> <strong>Last Updated:</strong> @DateTime.Now.ToString("MMMM dd, yyyy")</small>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .cu-card li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .cu-card li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
</style>
